 - **Architecture**: `Jenkinsfile.architecture` publishes producer `elasticsearch-deploy` (D50).
+- **Setup Job**: `elasticsearch-setup-<hash>` (`chart/templates/elasticsearch-setup-job.yaml`)
+  sets the built-in users' passwords and creates the users below. Its name hashes its whole
+  spec, so any change to the spec (the image pin included) is a new Job, which runs once;
+  Argo CD prunes the previous one.
+
+## The read-only user `reader`
+
+The setup Job creates Elasticsearch user `reader` with the built-in `viewer` role: it reads every
+index, through the API and in Kibana (`http://kibana.home`), and writes or manages nothing. Its
+password lives in OpenBao at `kv/eso/prd/elasticsearch/prd/filebeat-reader`, property
+`password`; ExternalSecret `elasticsearch-reader` materialises it as Secret
+`elasticsearch-reader`, which the Job reads as `READER_PASSWORD`. Nothing in this repository
+holds the value.
+
+Rotate the password as follows, with `bao` logged in and `kubectl` holding write access to the
+prd cluster. Nothing re-applies a changed password on its own: ESO refreshes
+the Secret only hourly, and Argo CD does not recreate a deleted Job by itself (the app
+auto-syncs with `selfHeal: false`, and auto-sync does not re-sync a revision it has already
+synced).
+
+1. Write the new value from stdin, so it never lands in a shell history:
+
+   ```sh
+   printf %s "$VALUE" | bao kv put -mount=kv eso/prd/elasticsearch/prd/filebeat-reader password=-
+   ```
+
+2. Make ESO refresh the Secret now, and wait until its last sync is later than step 1. A Job
+   that runs before then applies the old password again.
+
+   ```sh
+   kubectl -n elasticsearch-prd annotate externalsecret elasticsearch-reader force-sync=$(date +%s) --overwrite
+   kubectl -n elasticsearch-prd get externalsecret elasticsearch-reader \
+     -o jsonpath='{.status.refreshTime} {.status.conditions[?(@.type=="Ready")].status}{"\n"}'
+   ```
+
+3. Delete the completed setup Job:
+
+   ```sh
+   kubectl -n elasticsearch-prd get jobs -o name | grep '/elasticsearch-setup-' \
+     | xargs kubectl -n elasticsearch-prd delete
+   ```
+
+4. Start a sync of `elasticsearch-prd`: the Argo CD UI's **Sync** on the app. It recreates the
+   Job under the same name, and the Job sets the new password.
+5. Check that the Job completed (`kubectl -n elasticsearch-prd get jobs`) and that the new
+   password authenticates:
+
+   ```sh
+   curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -u "reader:$VALUE" http://elasticsearch.home/_security/_authenticate
+   ```
+
+   `200` means Elasticsearch is on the new password.
 
